(PRC-58 — before any successful reap, `the reaped status` is -1, a sentinel
 no real wait4 status word can take.
 Also covers: PRC-57 (it reflects the most recent SUCCESSFUL reap — a reap
 that fails leaves it alone, so it is still -1 after the failed one).
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-58.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   before any reap it is -1
   the failed reap set the error flag
   after a FAILED reap it is still -1
   after a successful reap it decodes to 8
)
print "before any reap it is {the reaped status}".
a number called 'the foreign reap' is reap process 999999.
On error print "the failed reap set the error flag".
print "after a FAILED reap it is still {the reaped status}".
a number called 'the child' is fork the process.
If 'the child' is 0 then, Exit 8.
a number called reaped is reap child 'the child'.
print "after a successful reap it decodes to {the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256}".
